  "report_period": "Week 42 (10th Oct to 17th Oct 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Hebei No. 1\" 182/2009 Dalian, China (SS 10/2029, DD 09/2027, Scrubber fitted) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 25 mill. Remind you that back in July, the two-years-younger sister vessel \"Pacific North\" 180/2011 Dalian, China (SS/DD 12/2025, Scrubber fitted) was sold at xs USD 25 mill. Sea Pioneer Shipping committed the Kamsarmax \"Generosity\" 83/2011 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 05/2028, DD 11/2026) to Greek interests at USD 17 mill. Note that a month ago, the one-year-older \"Eternal Bliss\" 82/2010 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 01/2030, DD 01/2028) was sold at USD 16,8 mill. The Panamax \"Tasik Sakura\" 76/2011 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 01/2026) was committed to Greek interests at low-mid USD 15 mill, while the one-year- older sister vessel \"Sunshine Bliss\" 76/2010 Oshima, Japan (SS 02/2030, DD 01/2028, Scrubber fitted) was sold a month ago at high USD 15 mill. On the Supramax sector, Jinhui Shipping & Trans committed the \"Jin Mao\" 56/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 05/2027) to Chinese interests at USD 13,1 mill. Note that back in July, the sister vessel \"Epic Trader\" 56/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS 08/2027, DD 10/2025) was sold at the same levels. Far East Shipping & Trading committed the OHBS Handysize \"La Bamba\" 37/2012 Saiki, Japan (SS/DD 04/2027) to Vietnamese interests at mid-high USD 14 mill. Remind you that the one-year-older sister vessel \"Wooyang Queen\" 37/2011 Saiki, Japan (SS/DD 08/2026, OHBS) was sold back in July at USD 13,8 mill.",
    "tankers": "Mercuria Energy Group committed the Suezmax \"Oceanus\" 150/2008 Universal, Japan (SS 04/2028, DD 07/2026, Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 38 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Samurai\" 150/2009 Universal, Japan (SS 02/2029, DD 03/2027, Scrubber fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 39,5 mill. Minerva Marine have sold their Aframax \"Minerva Lisa\" 103/2004 Samsung, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 10/2027, Ice Class 1C) to Chinese interests at USD 21,5 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the \"Apsogos\" 115/2004 Samsung, Korea (SS 07/2029, DD 11/2027) was sold at USD 22 mill. The MR2 \"Stavanger Poseidon\" 50/2020 Hyundai Vietnam, Vietnam (SS 08/2030, DD 10/2028, Scrubber fitted) of DSD Shipping was committed to Pakistan National Shipping Corp at USD 44,15 mill. For reference, the \"STI Maestro\" 47/2020 Hyundai Vietnam, Vietnam (SS 01/2030, DD 12/2027, Scrubber fitted) was sold back in August at USD 42 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 15,000/17,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 16,000/19,000 pd range. Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/18,000 pd. Indian coastal trips were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. South African trips into India were reported at the level of usd 13,000/14,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 300K/400K. Inter- Continental trips via US East Coast-US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via Black Sea into South East Asia were fixed around usd 25,000/27,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 600K/800K. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 25,000/26,000 pd. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 16,000 pd for 6/8 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Panamax was fixed on a period at the usd 14,000 pd basis delivery China for 4/6 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 15,000/16,000 pd. Trips from Japan via Far East into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Chinese trips into East Africa were fixed around usd 12,000/13,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 12,000/14,000 pd range. Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. India trips via South Africa into China were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 16,000/17,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips via East Coast India into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 12,000/13,000 pd. West African trips into India were reported at the level of usd 25,000/27,000 pd. South America coastal trips were fixed around usd 22,000/24,000 pd. South American trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 22,000/24,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/700K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from Red Sea into China-Japan range were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Continental trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 19,000/21,000 pd. US Gulf trips into West Coast Central America were reported at the level of usd 27,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 24,000/25,000 pd. East Coast South American and North Coast South American trips into West Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 30,000/33,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
